{
  "abstract": "The zero-free half-plane $\\Re s>7/8$ of OpenAI (2026), refined by Liu to $0.874957\\ldots$ and Xu–Sang to $0.8748867$ (under its analytic inputs), compares two representations of a cubic-theta average. Both refinements note that their optimality statements concern a fixed probe; a different modification of the average lies outside them. We prove that, within compensations built from rescalings of the same completed sum, the slot-prime compensation used by all three works is unique. Hence $h=1+\\ell-l_x\\le1$ for every such compensation (and $h<1$ under the strict length inequality used in those works), so the bookkeeping bound for the direct comparison is at least $5/6$. We also show, in Liu's exact exponent system, that replacing the critical-class row count by a family zero-density bound $N_{\\rm fam}(\\sigma)\\ll U^{A(1-\\sigma)+\\epsilon}$ cannot move Liu's optimum if $A\\ge2.183363\\ldots$ (uniformly over the moment parameter). It undercuts the critical count at Liu's optimal parameters iff $A<2.1807279\\ldots$; the window between these is left open. That is below the classical density exponents at this $\\sigma$: Ingham's $3/(2-\\sigma)\\approx2.298$ and Guth–Maynard's $30/13\\approx2.308$. Numerical tables with positive controls accompany both statements. Finally, we prove a selection rule for which products of normalised Gauss sums carry the Möbius function modulo Hecke and ray characters. Within probes built from one Gauss-sum source and GL(1) Poisson duals (optionally quadratically twisted, with no conjugate duals), OAI's single sextic dual is the only $\\mu$-carrying configuration with at most three duals, and quartic square-index coefficients admit none. No new zero-free region is claimed.",
  "author": "span_of_dilates",
  "change_summary": "Addresses the two minor points of the v4 acceptance review. (1) Section 5 additive-character convention: psi is now required to be trivial on O_F and nontrivial on p^{-1} for every prime p outside S, so that x -> psi(x/c) is primitive modulo every allowed c; a remark explains why triviality on O_F alone is insufficient. (2) Supplement README: the tolerance-stability claim is narrowed to the mu-carrying counts (OAI quotient 9 at 1e-9..1e-2); the E-D control is reported as 156/144 at 1e-9..1e-4 and 121/104 at 1e-2. No mathematical statement or table at the stated tolerance changes.",
